  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "It is morning in the kitchen. Grandma makes breakfast. Tom and Lily sit at the table. \"I have bread and eggs,\" says Grandma. \"I have green beans, too.\" Tom eats his bread. He drinks his milk. \"Lily, eat your breakfast,\" says Grandma. The beans are on a big plate. Lily looks at the beans.",
      "\"I do not like beans,\" says Lily. \"They are small and green.\" \"I like beans!\" says Tom. He eats six beans. \"Beans are good for your body,\" says Grandma. \"Try one bean, Lily.\" Lily does not want to try. Pip sits under the table. He looks at the floor.",
      "Lily picks up one bean. She puts it in her mouth. \"Oh!\" says Lily. \"It is nice!\" Grandma smiles at Lily. \"Can I have two beans?\" asks Lily. \"Yes, you can,\" says Grandma. One bean is on the floor. Pip eats it. Lily is happy. \"Pip likes beans too!\" says Tom."
    ],
    "summary": "Lily does not want to eat the green beans at breakfast. Grandma says to try one, and Lily likes it.",
